<title>INDONESIA: Indonesia raises March crude palm oil export tax.</title>
<headline>Indonesia raises March crude palm oil export tax.</headline>
<dateline>JAKARTA 1997-03-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indonesia's export tax on crude palm oil has been raised to $52.52 per tonne in March from $47.84 in February, the Finance Ministry said on Monday.</p>
<p>The tax on palm olein had been increased to $65.10 per tonne in March from $64.40, while that on RBD palm oil was raised to $55.64 in March from $52.52. The tax on crude olein had been increased to $63.70 in March from $63.05.</p>
<p>The export taxes, introduced in September 1994, are based on a composite average of international prices in the last two weeks of the previous month and are aimed at ensuring sufficient supply and stable prices in the domestic market.</p>
</text>
